// The syntax reference. scripts/build-docs.mjs turns this file into the docs page, llms-full.txt,
// the LLM prompt and the agent skill, and the golden tests check every answer, so the docs can't drift.
// "// ## Title" starts a section; other "//" lines are its description.

// ## Basics
// Type a calculation on any line; its answer appears beside it. Decimals are exact.
2 + 3 × 4 => 14
(2 + 3) × 4 => 20
2^10 => 1,024
10 mod 3 => 1
5! => 120
0.1 + 0.2 => 0.3

// ## Numbers
// Thousands separators, shorthands, other bases and fractions all work.
1,000,000 + 1_000 => 1,001,000
1.5k + 2M => 2,001,500
3bn / 1 million => 3,000
1.5e3 => 1,500
0xFF + 0b1010 => 265
1½ => 1.5

// ## Text and structure
// Words around numbers are ignored, so notes read naturally. Text before a colon is a label. Lines starting with # are headings, and // starts a comment.
3 apples + 2 apples => 5
rent: 1,200 => 1,200
5 plus 3 times 2 => 11
10 divided by 4 => 2.5

// ## Variables
// Name a value with =. Names can have spaces.
monthly rent = 1,200 => 1,200
utilities = 150 => 150
(monthly rent + utilities) × 12 => 16,200

// ## Previous answers and totals
// prev is the last answer. sum, avg, count, min and max cover the lines since the last heading or blank line. line3 is the answer on line 3.
groceries: 80 => 80
gas: 45 => 45
dinner: 55 => 55
sum => 180
avg => 60
prev × 2 => 120

// ## Percentages
20% of 50 => 10
50 + 10% => 55
10% off $80 => $72.00
5 as % of 20 => 25%
5 is what % of 20 => 25%
20% of what is 5 => 25

// ## Units
// Convert with in, to or as. Units combine and cancel, and plain numbers take the other side's unit.
5 km in miles => 3.1069 mi
6 ft 2 in in cm => 187.96 cm
72 °F in °C => 22.2222 °C
2 cups in ml => 473.1765 mL
1 GB / 4 MB => 250
60 mph in km/h => 96.5606 km/h
3 m × 4 m => 12 m²
1 m + 20 cm => 1.2 m
12pt in px => 16 px

// ## Money
// Currency symbols, codes and names, plus crypto. Rates refresh hourly and keep working offline; these examples use sample rates.
$30 in EUR => €27.00
€20 + $5 => €24.50
hourly rate = $85/h => $85.00/h
37.5 h × hourly rate => $3,187.50
0.01 BTC in USD => $1,000.00

// ## Dates and times
// These examples assume it's Thursday, Jan 15, 2026, 12:00 in UTC.
today + 2 weeks => Thu, Jan 29
next friday at 3pm => Fri, Jan 16, 3:00 PM
days until Dec 25 => 344 days
Jan 31 + 1 month => Sat, Feb 28
3pm + 90 min => 4:30 PM
3 days ago => Mon, Jan 12

// ## Time zones
// Use places (every major city), abbreviations like PST, or offsets like UTC+5:30.
time in Tokyo => 9:00 PM GMT+9
3pm PST in London => 11:00 PM GMT
9:00 EST to CET => 3:00 PM GMT+1

// ## Functions and formats
sqrt(16) + cbrt(27) => 7
round(3.14159, 2) => 3.14
sin(30) => 0.5
log(1000) => 3
2pi => 6.2831853072
255 in hex => 0xFF
1500 in sci => 1.5e3
